{"c":[{"id":"009e4aa697218076","sum":"All app builds run scripts/privacy_gate.sh: it needs pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation in helper/src/privacy/accepted.ts and onboarding showing Resources/PrivacyPromise.txt; refuses CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI. Release children get CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T001204Z-bb38791614f982ff","text":"Caret app builds, including Debug, run scripts/privacy_gate.sh; helper/src/privacy/accepted.ts must record lead acceptance of pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation before builds pass, and CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 is refused at build time.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T002947Z-c019705c5089f866","text":"The privacy gate also covers apps/caret/scripts/build-app.sh and direct helper bundling; onboarding must render generated Contents/Resources/PrivacyPromise.txt. Release child environments set CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1, which refuses every Vercel route even with a dev opt-in.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ceaba173a4e941d3","sum":"Xcode's privacy phases check source then processed plists; release env-file extraction keeps TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap only. Disclosure.walk refuses body keys with spaces (use note_1); dynamic-key state maps need a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T004510Z-16ddc03f0a00f357","text":"Xcode's first privacy phase checks source plists; its last requires the processed bundle plist as an input. Release helper env-file extraction preserves TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap and refuses other providers before spawn.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T030901Z-9525a678a3afd6cf","text":"Disclosure.walk refuses any request-body key outside KEY (no spaces), so ids like 'note 1' cannot be state keys (INT1 uses note_1); a state map with dynamic keys also needs a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts besides its .* row.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
